From 047e0487e6bbfd6104a8d5227d40cef55968188b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: scott <scott@chatcode.local>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 18:48:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] S2 glyph CNN: numpy-only classifier, segmentation, trained
 recipe, honest numbers (t-20261011-f0d2)

The learned reader, from scratch, numpy + PIL only (no torch, no pretrained):
- readers/glyphcnn.py: conv/pool/dense forward+backward in numpy, Adam with
  cosine decay, save/load. ~63k params.
- readers/segmentation.py: polarity -> Otsu -> deskew -> text bands -> glyph
  boxes with word-gap detection; shared by training and reading so train/test
  see the same normalisation.
- readers/cnn_reader.py: image -> text, bench-protocol stdout, --debug shows
  per-glyph confidences.
- tools/train_glyphs.py: data is GENERATED, never committed; when generator.py
  is present it harvests its sheets through the same segmenter the reader uses
  and DROPS mis-segmented sheets (never relabels them).
- tests/test_glyphcnn.py: 8 tests incl. finite-difference gradient check in
  float64, a naive-convolution reference, segmentation assertions and an
  end-to-end smoke (trains a tiny model in a tmpdir and reads a rendered word).
- models/glyphcnn.npz (234 KB, committed - under the 10 MB rule) + recipes/
  glyphcnn.json (seed, sizes, measured accuracy, architecture).
- reports/cnn-baseline.md: the honest numbers and the failure gallery.

Measured, not asserted: easy 7/30 (23.33%, bar 98), hard 11/180 (6.11%, bar
95), per-glyph 89.2%, median 0.211s per image. Eight of twelve hard families
fail at SEGMENTATION (0%), which is S3's job, not the classifier's. Two real
bugs found by tests on the way: im2col transposing after reshape (forward was
wrong, dw consistent, only a naive reference catches it) and ink polarity
decided after contrast stretching (selected the background). Full detail in
reports/cnn-baseline.md; raw run JSONs under reports/runs/.
